# Acceptance Criteria

## US-01 Online Product Purchase

### AC-01-01

**Given:** the customer is viewing the product list.

**When:** the customer searches for and selects a product.

**Then:** the system should display the selected product.

### AC-01-02

**Given:** the customer has selected a product.

**When:** the customer clicks the "Buy" option.

**Then:** the system should proceed with the purchase process.

### AC-01-03

**Given:** the customer has selected a product and proceeded with the purchase.

**When:** the customer completes the payment.

**Then:** the system should process the payment.

### AC-01-04

**Given:** the customer has completed a successful payment.

**When:** the payment is confirmed.

**Then:** the system should place the order.

---

## US-02 Account Creation and Login

### AC-02-01

**Given:** the customer does not have an account.

**When:** the customer enters valid account details and completes the verification code.

**Then:** the system should create the customer account.

### AC-02-02

**Given:** the customer has a registered account.

**When:** the customer enters valid login credentials.

**Then:** the system should allow the customer to log in.

### AC-02-03

**Given:** the customer enters an incorrect password.

**When:** the customer selects "Change Password".

**Then:** the system should start the password change process.

### AC-02-04

**Given:** the customer has selected the password change option.

**When:** the customer provides the registered email ID.

**Then:** the system should request the verification code.

### AC-02-05

**Given:** the customer has provided the registered email ID and valid verification code.

**When:** the customer enters a new password.

**Then:** the system should allow the customer to create the new password.

### AC-02-06

**Given:** the customer has successfully created a new password.

**When:** the customer logs in using the newly created password.

**Then:** the system should allow the customer to log in.

---

## US-03 Product Search and Category Navigation

### AC-03-01

**Given:** the customer is on the product search page.

**When:** the customer enters a keyword.

**Then:** the system should search for products matching the keyword.

### AC-03-02

**Given:** the customer is on the product search page.

**When:** the customer enters a model number.

**Then:** the system should search for products matching the model number.

### AC-03-03

**Given:** the customer is viewing the product categories.

**When:** the customer selects a category.

**Then:** the system should display the products under that category.

### AC-03-04

**Given:** the customer has searched for a product or selected a category.

**When:** the search or category selection is completed.

**Then:** the system should display the relevant products.

---

## US-04 Add Product to Cart

### AC-04-01

**Given:** the customer is viewing an available product.

**When:** the customer clicks "Add to Cart".

**Then:** the system should add the selected product to the cart.

### AC-04-02

**Given:** the customer has selected a product.

**When:** the customer clicks "Add to Cart".

**Then:** the selected product should be added to the cart.

### AC-04-03

**Given:** a product has been added to the cart.

**When:** the customer opens "My Cart".

**Then:** the added product should be displayed in the cart.

---

## US-05 Product Quantity and Availability

### AC-05-01

**Given:** the customer is viewing a product.

**When:** the product availability is checked.

**Then:** the system should display the product availability.

### AC-05-02

**Given:** a product is in stock.

**When:** the customer views the product.

**Then:** the "Add to Cart" and "Buy" options should be enabled.

### AC-05-03

**Given:** a product is out of stock.

**When:** the customer views the product.

**Then:** the "Add to Cart" and "Buy" options should be disabled.

### AC-05-04

**Given:** the product is available for purchase.

**When:** the customer selects the required quantity.

**Then:** the system should allow the customer to select the required quantity.

### AC-05-05

**Given:** the product is available and the required quantity has been selected.

**When:** the customer clicks "Buy".

**Then:** the system should proceed with the purchase process.

---

## US-06 Delivery Address

### AC-06-01

**Given:** the customer is on the delivery information page.

**When:** the customer enters a valid name.

**Then:** the system should accept the name.

### AC-06-02

**Given:** the customer is on the delivery information page.

**When:** the customer enters a valid delivery address.

**Then:** the system should accept the delivery address.

### AC-06-03

**Given:** the customer is on the delivery information page.

**When:** the customer enters a valid phone number.

**Then:** the system should accept the phone number.

### AC-06-04

**Given:** the customer has registered account details.

**When:** the customer opens the delivery information page.

**Then:** the system should populate the name and phone number from the account details.

### AC-06-05

**Given:** the customer has entered the delivery information.

**When:** the customer reviews the information.

**Then:** the system should display the delivery information for review.

### AC-06-06

**Given:** the customer has entered and reviewed the delivery information.

**When:** the customer submits the delivery information.

**Then:** the system should allow the customer to proceed to payment.

---

## US-07 Online Payment and Order Summary

### AC-07-01

**Given:** the customer has completed the delivery information.

**When:** the customer clicks "Pay".

**Then:** the system should start the payment process.

### AC-07-02

**Given:** the customer has selected the payment option.

**When:** the customer proceeds with payment.

**Then:** the system should navigate to the payment portal.

### AC-07-03

**Given:** the customer is on the payment portal.

**When:** the customer completes the payment.

**Then:** the system should process the payment.

### AC-07-04

**Given:** the payment has been successfully processed.

**When:** the payment confirmation is received.

**Then:** the system should display "Payment Successful".

### AC-07-05

**Given:** the customer has completed the payment successfully.

**When:** the payment is confirmed.

**Then:** the system should place the order.

### AC-07-06

**Given:** the order has been successfully placed.

**When:** the payment is confirmed.

**Then:** the system should display the order summary.

### AC-07-07

**Given:** the order has been successfully placed.

**When:** the order summary is generated.

**Then:** the system should share the order summary with the customer's registered email ID.

### AC-07-08

**Given:** the payment is unsuccessful.

**When:** the payment attempt fails.

**Then:** the system should not place the order.

### AC-07-09

**Given:** the payment attempt is unsuccessful.

**When:** the payment fails.

**Then:** the system should display an appropriate "Payment Failed" or error message.

### AC-07-10

**Given:** the payment attempt has failed.

**When:** the customer chooses to retry the payment.

**Then:** the system should allow the customer to return to the Delivery Address page and retry the payment.

---

## US-08 Order Processing Notification

### AC-08-01

**Given:** an order has been successfully placed.

**When:** order processing starts.

**Then:** the system should notify the Store Executive.

### AC-08-02

**Given:** an order has been successfully placed.

**When:** order processing starts.

**Then:** the system should notify the Delivery Partner.

### AC-08-03

**Given:** an order has been successfully placed.

**When:** the Store Executive is notified.

**Then:** the Store Executive should receive the order details required for packing.

### AC-08-04

**Given:** an order has been successfully placed.

**When:** the Delivery Partner is notified.

**Then:** the Delivery Partner should receive the order details required for delivery.

### AC-08-05

**Given:** an order has been successfully placed.

**When:** the order confirmation is completed.

**Then:** order processing should start.

---

## US-09 Order Tracking

### AC-09-01

**Given:** the customer has successfully placed an order.

**When:** the order is confirmed.

**Then:** the system should provide the Order ID.

### AC-09-02

**Given:** the customer has an Order ID.

**When:** the customer opens the Tracking tab.

**Then:** the system should display the order tracking option.

### AC-09-03

**Given:** the customer is on the Tracking tab.

**When:** the customer enters the Order ID.

**Then:** the system should retrieve the corresponding order.

### AC-09-04

**Given:** a valid Order ID has been entered.

**When:** the system retrieves the order.

**Then:** the system should display the current delivery status.

### AC-09-05

**Given:** the customer is tracking an order.

**When:** the order status is updated.

**Then:** the tracking information should display the applicable delivery status.

---

## US-10 Delivery Status Update

### AC-10-01

**Given:** the Delivery Partner is handling an order.

**When:** the delivery status changes.

**Then:** the Delivery Partner should update the delivery status.

### AC-10-02

**Given:** the Delivery Partner has updated the delivery status.

**When:** the status update is saved.

**Then:** the Store Executive should be able to view the updated delivery status.

### AC-10-03

**Given:** the delivery status has been updated.

**When:** the customer checks the order tracking.

**Then:** the customer should be able to view the updated delivery status.

### AC-10-04

**Given:** the product has been successfully delivered.

**When:** the Delivery Partner updates the delivery status.

**Then:** the system should update the status to "Delivered".

### AC-10-05

**Given:** a relevant delivery status has changed.

**When:** the status update is recorded.

**Then:** the system should notify the Store Executive and Delivery Partner.

### AC-10-06

**Given:** the customer is unavailable during delivery.

**When:** the Delivery Partner attempts the delivery.

**Then:** the Delivery Partner should attempt to contact the customer.

### AC-10-07

**Given:** the customer is unavailable during the delivery attempt.

**When:** the applicable process requires another attempt.

**Then:** the delivery should be reattempted according to the applicable process.

### AC-10-08

**Given:** the specified delivery attempts have failed.

**When:** the applicable failed-delivery process is completed.

**Then:** the product should be returned to the store.

### AC-10-09

**Given:** the product has been returned to the store.

**When:** the return is recorded.

**Then:** the system should cancel the order.

### AC-10-10

**Given:** the order is cancelled because the customer was unavailable.

**When:** the cancellation is processed.

**Then:** the payment should not be refunded.

---

## US-11 Return Refund or Exchange

### AC-11-01

**Given:** the customer has a purchased product.

**When:** the customer selects "Return/Refund".

**Then:** the system should start the return/refund process.

### AC-11-02

**Given:** the customer has selected "Return/Refund".

**When:** the customer starts the request.

**Then:** the system should check the return/refund eligibility period.

### AC-11-03

**Given:** the return/refund eligibility period has expired.

**When:** the customer attempts to submit a return/refund request.

**Then:** the system should display an appropriate message.

### AC-11-04

**Given:** the product is within the return/refund eligibility period.

**When:** the eligibility check is successful.

**Then:** the system should allow the customer to proceed to the Return/Refund page.

### AC-11-05

**Given:** the product is eligible for return/refund.

**When:** the customer reaches the Return/Refund page.

**Then:** the customer should be able to select Return, Refund, or Exchange.

### AC-11-06

**Given:** the customer has selected Return, Refund, or Exchange.

**When:** the customer submits the request.

**Then:** the customer should be able to provide a reason.

### AC-11-07

**Given:** supporting evidence is required for the request.

**When:** the customer submits the request.

**Then:** the customer should be able to upload the required evidence.

### AC-11-08

**Given:** the customer has provided the required request details.

**When:** the customer submits the request.

**Then:** the system should submit the return/refund/exchange request.

### AC-11-09

**Given:** a return/refund/exchange request has been submitted.

**When:** the request is recorded.

**Then:** the system should notify the Store Executive and Delivery Partner.

### AC-11-10

**Given:** the Store Executive has received a return/refund/exchange request.

**When:** the Store Executive reviews the request.

**Then:** the Store Executive should be able to approve or reject the request.

### AC-11-11

**Given:** a product return has been approved and collection is required.

**When:** the return collection is initiated.

**Then:** the Delivery Partner should collect the product.

### AC-11-12

**Given:** the returned product has been collected.

**When:** the product reaches the required verification stage.

**Then:** the returned product should be checked.

### AC-11-13

**Given:** the returned product has been checked.

**When:** the Store Executive completes the review.

**Then:** the Store Executive should process the applicable return, refund, or exchange.

---

## US-12 Return Refund Status Tracking

### AC-12-01

**Given:** the customer has a return/refund request.

**When:** the customer opens the Tracking tab.

**Then:** the system should display the tracking option.

### AC-12-02

**Given:** the customer is on the Tracking tab.

**When:** the customer enters the existing Order ID.

**Then:** the system should retrieve the corresponding return/refund request.

### AC-12-03

**Given:** a valid Order ID has been entered.

**When:** the system retrieves the return/refund request.

**Then:** the system should display the current return/refund status.

### AC-12-04

**Given:** a return/refund request has been submitted.

**When:** the request is created.

**Then:** the system should display the status as "Return/Refund Requested".

### AC-12-05

**Given:** a return/refund request is being processed.

**When:** the request moves through the applicable stages.

**Then:** the system should update the status through the approval, collection, and refund stages.

### AC-12-06

**Given:** the return/refund/exchange process has been completed.

**When:** the applicable final action is completed.

**Then:** the system should display "Refund Provided" or "Exchange Completed".

### AC-12-07

**Given:** a return/refund request is in progress.

**When:** the request moves to the next stage.

**Then:** the system should update the status accordingly.